    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "In the summers of 1994/95, 1995/96, 1996/97 and 1997/98, researchers visited\nthe waters of Patagonian Channels, Drake Passage, Bransfield Strait and de\nGerlache Strait looking for cetaceans. The observations were made from the\nbridge of Chilean Navy Ships ISAZA and MICALVI during the tracks for logistic\nsupport to INACH and specially dedicated tracks for cetaceans. The objectives\nof this were identifying cetaceans species mainly from Antarctic Peninsula and\ntheir summer distribution",
